invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_word.h
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the row of a product returns the word above its four without the
  carry out of the high halves' chain, so a product whose chain carried
  is short by 2^256 at that row. Nothing faults: uint64_t arithmetic
  defines every wrap, and the field and the scalar both go on computing
  with a wrong value. bin/p256_equiv_test holds every product to
  p256_field.c's and p256_scalar.c's.

--- old
    return (uint64_t)(p3 >> 64) + low_carry + high_carry;
--- new
    return (uint64_t)(p3 >> 64) + low_carry;
